  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3128",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3128: Important priority package update for curl",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-09-28 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-28 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-80230:\n\tWhen CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY is configured alongside options that disable standard peer verification (CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = 0 and CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST = 0), libcurl fails to enforce public key pinning on connections established without a presented server certificate. Bypassing the pinning check under these disabled-verification conditions allows unauthenticated connections to succeed when they should be rejected.\n",
